+#### signal
+
+Type: [`AbortSignal`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal)
+
+Cancel queued tasks when the signal is aborted.
+
+Pending tasks are rejected with the signal's abort reason, and any task added after the abort is rejected without ever running.
+
+Note: This does not cancel tasks that are already running.
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 2, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const promises = urls.map(url => limit(() => fetch(url, {signal: controller.signal})));
+
+controller.abort();
+```
+
 ### limit(fn, ...args)

 Returns the promise returned by calling `fn(...args)`.
